# Korva Comply — Project Rules

## Stack

- Next.js 14 (App Router)
- TypeScript (strict)
- Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth + Row Level Security)
- Zendesk Apps Framework (ZAF) for Zendesk integration
- Anthropic Claude API (claude-sonnet-4-20250514) for classification
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Vercel for deployment

## Naming

- Product name: Korva Comply
- Database tables use snake_case
- API routes under /api/
- Zendesk custom fields prefixed with korva_comply_

## Key Constraints

- NEVER store full ticket content in our database (GDPR)
- Store only classification results, metadata, and audit trail
- All Zendesk API auth via OAuth 2.0, never API tokens
- EU hosting only (Supabase EU region, Vercel EU)
- Every classification decision must be logged with timestamp and actor
